Q: Get unlimited row count and paginated results from the database using CodeIgniter A: <p>To avoid writing most of the query builder calls in two separate places, some CodeIgniter developers opt to build the shared clauses, then clone that object then separately extend and execute the two queries (in a single model method).</p>
<p>Do not use <code>num_rows()</code> to access the row count because that query demands that the database return whole records - which you don't intend to use. Execute a COUNT() query with <code>count_all_results()</code>.</p>
<p>The call site for the following method should be written to access the dyadic, associative array returned.</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function getTotalRowsAndLimitedResults(int $id, ?int $limit, ?int $offset): array
{
    $this-&gt;db
        -&gt;from($this-&gt;db-&gt;dbprefix . 'page_to_category p2c', 'left')
        -&gt;join($this-&gt;db-&gt;dbprefix . 'page p', 'p.page_id = p2c.page_id', 'left')
        -&gt;join($this-&gt;db-&gt;dbprefix . 'page_description pd', 'pd.page_id = p2c.page_id', 'left')
        -&gt;or_where([
            'p2c.parent_id' =&gt; $id,
            'p2c.category_id' =&gt; $id,
         ]);

    $clone = clone $this-&gt;db;

    return [
        'total' =&gt; $this-&gt;db-&gt;count_all_results(),
        'result' =&gt; $clone-&gt;get('', $limit, $offset)-&gt;result_array(),
    ];
}
</code></pre>
